  "_doc": "normalize_painting_state (Python) and normalizePaintingState (JS) read the numbers of a stroke, its points and a raster object the same (docs/scene-state-v2.md, 共通の規則 and `painting`): only a finite JSON number counts, as for z_index; text (even \"3\" or \"\"), a boolean, a list and an infinity (a number too large for a double) are invalid. An invalid size, opacity, u, v or bbox value drops the stroke (raster object); an invalid createdAt and point t are 0, a color component r, g or b 0 and a 1, radiusValue null, widthScale and pressureLike absent, transform du, dv and rot_deg 0 and scale 1. A number too long for a double (a 400-digit integer) is an infinity. Each case patches one part of the base stroke (`stroke`, its first point `point`, its `color`) or raster object (`raster`, its `bbox`, its `transform`). `drop` lists keys removed from a part (missing). `expected` null means the stroke (raster object) is dropped; otherwise its listed keys are compared, `point` against the first point.",
